<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sunifred of Urgell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 848</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Sunifred I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sunifred was a 9th-century Frankish count who ruled Urgell and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a> from about 834 and also <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girona">Girona</a> and other counties of the Spanish March from 844 until his death in 848. He was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfred-the-hairy">Wilfred the Hairy</a> and the ancestor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-barcelona">House of Barcelona</a>, which ruled Catalonia for more than five centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sunifred-of-urgell.jpg" alt="Sunifred of Urgell" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: georg-hessen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Honors-sunifred-844-848.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
